0101_away_piles_wider — NOT CARRIED AS A STEP, AND NEVER WILL BE.

The shared entry only widens the closed set on `away_responders.piles`: DROP CONSTRAINT then ADD
CONSTRAINT, which Postgres allows and SQLite does not. A CHECK is part of the table definition
here, so changing one member would mean rebuilding the table.

There is nothing to rebuild. `piles` carries no CHECK on this store and `0096_away_piles.sql`
never gave it one — a widenable set is refused at the write door, not by the table. That is the
rule now, not a consequence of the journal being unreleased, so this entry stays a no-op however
many members the set gains. `closed-set-parity.test.ts` holds both halves.
